<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mangkunegara IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1811">1811</a>–<a href="/years/1881">1881</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mangkunegara IV was prince of the Mangkunegaran principality in Surakarta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, from 1853 to 1881. He made the house wealthy by building <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> mills and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> estates and reforming its finances. He was also a leading Javanese poet, author of the moral poem Serat Wedhatama, and a patron of court music and dance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mangkunegara-iv.jpg" alt="Mangkunegara IV" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mangkunegara_IV,_Southeast_Asian_and_Caribbean_Images,_Leiden_University_Libraries-KITLV.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
